<pending_commit branch="arc-12.1.0-pre2" change_id="Ie3c76b73aab94746d0a9c1ad20c5f636bb5a5930" commit="97f4d16b72ce840c2c58460333fcc74ded43715a" commit_message="UPSTREAM: mesa/get: Add TYPE_UINT for casting through a GLuint.  The &quot;State Tables&quot; section of the OpenGL specification lists many values as belonging to Z+ (non-negative integers), not Z (all integers).  For ordinary glGetInteger queries, this doesn't matter.  However, when accessing Z+ values via glGetFloat or glGetInteger64, we need to treat the source value as an unsigned value.  Otherwise, we'll produce a negative number when bit 31 is set.  This commit merely adds the plumbing.  It doesn't convert any values.  v2: Gotta catch 'em all (add missing cases caught by Ilia)  Signed-off-by: Kenneth Graunke &lt;kenneth@whitecape.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ilia Mirkin &lt;imirkin@alum.mit.edu&gt; (cherry picked from commit 9f93afb9a5586cb90e127ba7d63de3b416d08821)  Change-Id: Ie3c76b73aab94746d0a9c1ad20c5f636bb5a5930 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/423000 Commit-Ready: Haixia Shi &lt;hshi@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Haixia Shi &lt;hshi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Haixia Shi &lt;hshi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="423000" owner_email="hshi@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/mesa" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/mesa" ref="refs/changes/00/423000/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="arc-12.1.0-pre2" change_id="Ia41d2950afbd44e07e5d25748522c102edd83ea7" commit="68e5dc03815615687bd7e820e48d0caece1cc1bf" commit_message="UPSTREAM: mesa/get: Convert stencil values to TYPE_UINT.  These are listed as Z+ in the GL spec, and often have values of 0xFFFFFFFF.  For glGetFloat, we should return 4294967295.0 rather than -1.0.  Similarly, for glGetInteger64v, we should return 0xFFFFFFFF, not the sign extended 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF.  Fixes 6 dEQP tests matching the pattern dEQP-GLES3.functional.state_query.integers.stencil*value*mask*getfloat when run in a single process (with state reset code happening between tests, which makes dEQP set the stencil value mask to 0xFFFFFFFF).  Signed-off-by: Kenneth Graunke &lt;kenneth@whitecape.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ilia Mirkin &lt;imirkin@alum.mit.edu&gt; (cherry picked from commit 37d63b50b196afe61b4d7c33b1118a49a5e1e13f)  BUG=chrome-os-partner:61232 BUG=b:33816113 TEST=run cts -m CtsDeqpTestCases --skip-device-info --module-arg CtsDeqpTestCases:include-filter:dEQP-GLES3.functional.state_query.integers#stencil_*_getfloat  Change-Id: Ia41d2950afbd44e07e5d25748522c102edd83ea7 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/423001 Commit-Ready: Haixia Shi &lt;hshi@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Haixia Shi &lt;hshi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Haixia Shi &lt;hshi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="423001" owner_email="hshi@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/mesa" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/mesa" ref="refs/changes/01/423001/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2ed016d7a76d42996b2669b37c12f1263d776a27" commit="0a7e6fe94e8afde818e75c25a1b05b350805d8d1" commit_message="webservd: add native 64-bit syscalls  The syscall filter is written mostly for arm and is missing a bunch of syscalls used on native 64-bit arches like amd64.  Add them here.  BUG=None TEST=webservd doesn't crash on amd64-generic anymore  Change-Id: I2ed016d7a76d42996b2669b37c12f1263d776a27 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/424633 Commit-Ready: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Garret Kelly &lt;gdk@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="424633" owner_email="vapier@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="aosp/platform/system/webservd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/aosp/platform/system/webservd" ref="refs/changes/33/424633/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I46d9793da242b07aa03b4cb6b1eaf538319b097b" commit="407af3b9026b665dc02a32a132b7d01a3fdc386b" commit_message="CHROMIUM: atmel_mxt_ts: Add sysfs for requesting T19 status  T19 status can be used to differentiate the touch sensors that are attached to the touch controller. This CL adds a sysfs entry for 1) when written to, it requests the touch controller to report the T19    status 2) when read, it returns the latest T19 status  BUG=chrome-os-partner:29065 TEST=tested on clapper that the T19 status can be read as 0x3C, which represents the correct touch sensor.  Signed-off-by: Yufeng Shen &lt;miletus@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/200814 Reviewed-by: Andrew de los Reyes &lt;adlr@chromium.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Charlie Mooney &lt;charliemooney@chromium.org&gt;  Change-Id: I46d9793da242b07aa03b4cb6b1eaf538319b097b Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/422573 Commit-Ready: Charlie Mooney &lt;charliemooney@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Charlie Mooney &lt;charliemooney@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dtor@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="422573" owner_email="charliemooney@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/73/422573/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I46d9793da242b07aa03b4cb6b1eaf538319b097b" commit="2eb44a3c997570fff42a5bc2e00124d448e8ae3f" commit_message="CHROMIUM: atmel_mxt_ts: Add sysfs for requesting T19 status  T19 status can be used to differentiate the touch sensors that are attached to the touch controller. This CL adds a sysfs entry for 1) when written to, it requests the touch controller to report the T19    status 2) when read, it returns the latest T19 status  BUG=chrome-os-partner:29065 TEST=tested on clapper that the T19 status can be read as 0x3C, which represents the correct touch sensor.  Signed-off-by: Yufeng Shen &lt;miletus@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/200814 Reviewed-by: Andrew de los Reyes &lt;adlr@chromium.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Charlie Mooney &lt;charliemooney@chromium.org&gt;  Change-Id: I46d9793da242b07aa03b4cb6b1eaf538319b097b Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/422413 Commit-Ready: Charlie Mooney &lt;charliemooney@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Charlie Mooney &lt;charliemooney@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dtor@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="422413" owner_email="charliemooney@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/13/422413/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I5c507609899c25a86407dc8c8b3284e1d19399e1" commit="5b4ef590436340414929ee81235537a76a038f33" commit_message="CHROMIUM: LSM: Add support for symlink traversal policy.  This change adds functionality to the chromiumos LSM to pin inodes and associate tracking information with them. This allows tracking symlink traversal policy for an inode. Whenever the FS layer follows a link, it calls out to the LSM, which can then check whether a symlink traversal policy has been set on any directory on the path in question. If a policy is set and it specifies that symlink traversal should be blocked, the corresponding FS system call will fail with EPERM. Note that readlink() continues to work, so userspace may resort to resolving symlinks manually if desired.  Symlink traversal policy is configured via securityfs. Files in /sys/kernel/security/chromiumos/symlink_policy/ are used to set the symlink traversal policy:   * .../allow: Write a path to the file to set the symlink traversal     policy for corresponding inode to &quot;allow&quot;.   * .../block: Write a path to the file to set the symlink traversal     policy for corresponding inode to &quot;block&quot;.   * .../reset: Write a path to clear the symlink traversal policy for     the corresponding inode.   * .../flush: Write a path to clear symlink traversal policy for the     entire file system the corresponding inode belongs to. Note that     this may affect paths outside the subtree corresponding to the     specified path (e.g. parents, siblings, or parts of the file     system not visible in the affected (bind) mount).  BUG=chromium:655606 TEST=Set symlink traversal policy and test paths containing symlinks.  Change-Id: I5c507609899c25a86407dc8c8b3284e1d19399e1 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/420988 Commit-Ready: Mattias Nissler &lt;mnissler@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mattias Nissler &lt;mnissler@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dtor@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="420988" owner_email="mnissler@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/88/420988/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I0fc385b0f1914367ed2e9f4a24273e729ded3310" commit="1fe27cceb7604bc4db7a6fcaed52fde927a1252a" commit_message="telemetry_AFDOGenerate: collect perf.data with images by clang  The code layout can be quite different by gcc and clang/llvm. To make most of afdo, feedback file used by clang needs to be collected on images built by llvm.  BUG=chromium:676173 TEST=Run and check files on gs  Change-Id: I0fc385b0f1914367ed2e9f4a24273e729ded3310 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/422540 Commit-Ready: Ting-Yuan Huang &lt;laszio@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ting-Yuan Huang &lt;laszio@chromium.org&gt;